    <string name="cheats_onboarding_title">About the cheats tab</string>
    <string name="cheats_onboarding_slide1_title">Taps and lights</string>
    <string name="cheats_onboarding_slide1_body">Tap a button to fire the cheat. Lights come from the game itself, not from the tap, so a cheat that didn\'t take never looks like it did. The last refusal shows as a short red line at the bottom in the plugin\'s own words.</string>
    <string name="cheats_onboarding_slide2_title">Auto-apply on reconnect</string>
    <string name="cheats_onboarding_slide2_body">Toggles you turn on come back automatically when the companion reconnects (new session, game relaunch). Long-press a one-shot cheat to make it auto-fire too, as soon as the game is in a safe state. Turn the whole thing off in Settings &#8594; Cheats.</string>
    <string name="cheats_onboarding_next">Next</string>
    <string name="cheats_onboarding_done">Got it</string>

    <!-- HUD-page first-visit onboarding sheet. 3 slides on GTA IV
         (no Customs slide), 4 on GTA V. English only; translations
         are a follow-up. -->
    <string name="hud_onboarding_title">About the HUD</string>
    <string name="hud_onboarding_slide_hud_title">What you\'re looking at</string>
    <string name="hud_onboarding_slide_hud_body">Cards for cash, weapon and ammo, vehicle and speed, radio station, plus the health and armour bars along the bottom. Everything follows the game on its own.</string>
    <string name="hud_onboarding_slide_tap_title">Tap to act</string>
    <string name="hud_onboarding_slide_tap_body">Tap a radio station to retune it. Tap the weapon card on foot (or hold the weapon-wheel button on the controller) to pick a weapon.</string>
    <string name="hud_onboarding_slide_customs_title">Long-press the vehicle card</string>
    <string name="hud_onboarding_slide_customs_body">Sitting in a car? A long press on the vehicle card opens Customs: paint, parts, performance, wheels, tint, plate, neon. Look for the small pencil icon next to the vehicle name.</string>
    <string name="hud_onboarding_slide_ammu_title">Long-press the weapon card</string>
    <string name="hud_onboarding_slide_ammu_body">On foot? A long press on the weapon card opens Ammu-Nation: attachments, weapon tint, and refill ammo. Tap the card still opens the weapon wheel. Look for the small pencil icon next to the weapon name.</string>
    <string name="hud_onboarding_slide_tabs_title">More tabs</string>
    <string name="hud_onboarding_slide_tabs_body">Swipe left for the map (blips, one-tap routing) or right for cheats. The HUD stays in the middle so you always know how to get back.</string>

    <!-- Map-tab first-visit onboarding sheet. Three slides covering
         what the screen does, the pan/zoom/lock gestures, and the
         icon column that reaches the other tabs without leaving the
         map. English only; translations alongside. -->
    <string name="map_onboarding_title">About the map tab</string>
    <string name="map_onboarding_slide_overview_title">What this screen does</string>
    <string name="map_onboarding_slide_overview_body">Mirrors the game\'s minimap enlarged on the Thor\'s bottom screen. Tap start mirroring and allow screen capture when Android asks. Stop any time with the stop icon.</string>
    <string name="map_onboarding_slide_gestures_title">Pan, zoom, lock</string>
    <string name="map_onboarding_slide_gestures_body">Pinch to zoom and drag to pan the mirror until the framing feels right. The refresh icon snaps back to the default view. Tap the lock icon when you\'re happy so a stray touch doesn\'t throw it off.</string>
    <string name="map_onboarding_slide_actions_title">Icon shortcuts</string>
    <string name="map_onboarding_slide_actions_body">The icon column reaches the other tabs without leaving the map. Home for the HUD, dice for cheats, pin for blips, radio for stations. Driving overlays (speedometer, waypoint distance on V, routed destination) appear by themselves while you\'re in a car.</string>

